<div class="hc-topic" id="pn-account">
    <h3><x-icon name="user" /> Your panelist account</h3>
    <p>Your Administrator registers you in <strong>Panelist Management</strong> and gives you a username and a temporary password. By default:</p>
    <div class="hc-options">
        <div class="hc-option"><div class="hc-option-icon"><x-icon name="user" /></div><div><div class="hc-option-title">Username</div><p>Your first name in lower case, e.g. <code>maria</code>. A number is added if the name is taken: <code>maria2</code>.</p></div></div>
        <div class="hc-option"><div class="hc-option-icon"><x-icon name="key" /></div><div><div class="hc-option-title">Temporary password</div><p>Your first and last initials plus the school year's start year, e.g. <code>MS2026</code>.</p></div></div>
    </div>
    <p>Sign in and change the temporary password on first use — see <a href="#gs-first-login">Your first sign-in</a>. Your account belongs to the Administrator's college; you can be assigned to any of that college's categories.</p>
</div>

<div class="hc-topic" id="pn-dashboard">
    <h3><x-icon name="grid" /> Dashboard</h3>
    <figure class="hc-figure">
        <div class="hc-window">
            <div class="hc-window-bar"><div class="hc-window-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="hc-window-url">/panelist/dashboard</div></div>
            <div class="hc-screen is-flush">
                <div class="m-app">
                    <div class="m-side">
                        <div class="m-side-brand">ARPQRS</div>
                        <div class="m-nav is-on"><x-icon name="grid" /> Dashboard</div>
                        <div class="m-nav"><x-icon name="list-check" /> My Assignments</div>
                        <div class="m-nav"><x-icon name="calendar" /> View Schedule</div>
                        <div class="m-side-foot"><div class="m-nav"><x-icon name="settings" /> Settings</div></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="m-body">
                        <div class="m-top"><span class="m-title">Dashboard</span><span class="m-btn is-ghost"><x-icon name="help-circle" /> Help Center</span><span class="m-icon-btn"><x-icon name="bell" /><span class="m-count">2</span></span><span class="m-pin">1</span><span class="m-icon-btn"><x-icon name="qr-code" /></span><span class="m-pin">2</span></div>
                        <div class="m-page">
                            <div class="m-between"><span class="m-input" style="min-width:10rem">Capstone Final Defense ▾</span><span class="m-pin">3</span></div>
                            <div class="m-stats">
                                <div class="m-stat"><div class="m-label">Assigned</div><div class="m-stat-value">12</div></div>
                                <div class="m-stat"><div class="m-label">Completed</div><div class="m-stat-value">7</div></div>
                                <div class="m-stat"><div class="m-label">Pending</div><div class="m-stat-value">5</div></div>
                                <div class="m-stat"><div class="m-label">Upcoming</div><div class="m-stat-value">5</div></div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="m-card"><div class="m-between"><span class="m-label">Live Room Status · Room 101</span><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-success">Active</span></div><div class="m-small">Now: CFD-2026-0007 · Next: CFD-2026-0012</div></div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption><strong>Figure 8.</strong> The Panelist dashboard.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <ul class="hc-pins">
        <li><span class="m-pin">1</span><span><strong>Notifications</strong> — the number shows unread items.</span></li>
        <li><span class="m-pin">2</span><span><strong>Room Session</strong> — opens your phone camera to scan a room device's QR code.</span></li>
        <li><span class="m-pin">3</span><span><strong>Category</strong> — switch between the categories you serve on. Counts, the live room and announcements follow it.</span></li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class="hc-topic" id="pn-assignments">
    <h3><x-icon name="list-check" /> My Assignments</h3>
    <p>Every group you are seated on, in three tabs:</p>
    <div class="hc-panel">
        <div class="hc-legend-row"><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-brand">Scheduled</span><span>Still to present, <strong>nearest first</strong>. Times are live expected times while a day is running.</span></div>
        <div class="hc-legend-row"><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-danger">Deferred</span><span>Set aside, with the real time and reason. View only.</span></div>
        <div class="hc-legend-row"><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-success">Completed</span><span>Already presented, newest first, with the real completion time.</span></div>
    </div>
    <p>Each row's <strong>⋮</strong> menu offers <strong>View</strong> (the group's members, titles, room, time and your role). On a Completed row, View opens the <strong>evaluation sheet</strong> the panel submitted. On a Scheduled row you can also <strong>Mark Unavailable</strong>.</p>
    <p>Your role on each group is shown as <span class="hc-badge hc-badge-info">Lead Panelist</span>, <span class="hc-badge hc-badge-muted">Member</span> or <span class="hc-badge hc-badge-brand">Backup Panelist</span> — see <a href="#pn-roles">Lead Panelist, Member and Backup</a>.</p>
</div>

<div class="hc-topic" id="pn-unavailable">
    <h3><x-icon name="user-x" /> Marking yourself unavailable</h3>
    <p>If you cannot sit on a scheduled group, open its <strong>⋮</strong> menu in My Assignments and choose <strong>Mark Unavailable</strong>. This sends a report to your Administrator, who chooses your replacement.</p>
    <ol class="hc-steps">
        <li class="hc-step"><div class="hc-step-marker">1</div><div class="hc-step-body"><div class="hc-step-head">Report</div><div class="hc-result">Row <x-icon name="arrow-right" /> <span class="hc-badge hc-badge-warn">Pending Review</span></div></div></li>
        <li class="hc-step"><div class="hc-step-marker">2</div><div class="hc-step-body"><div class="hc-step-head">The Administrator assigns a replacement</div><p class="hc-step-text">You get a notification "Marked unavailable for … Approved by …" and the group leaves your Scheduled list.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="hc-note hc-note-warn"><x-icon name="alert-triangle" /><p>Until a replacement is assigned you are still on the panel. Report as early as possible, and tell your Administrator directly if the presentation is today.</p></div>
</div>

<div class="hc-topic" id="pn-notifications">
    <h3><x-icon name="bell" /> Notifications</h3>
    <p>The <x-icon name="bell" style="width:.9em;height:.9em;vertical-align:-.1em" /> bell in the top bar lists what changed for you, newest first, each with its date and time. Clicking one marks it read and, where it applies, takes you to My Assignments with the affected rows highlighted.</p>
    <div class="hc-options">
        <div class="hc-option"><div class="hc-option-icon is-success"><x-icon name="user-plus" /></div><div><div class="hc-option-title">New assignment</div><p>You were added to a panel — "Assigned to 3 groups." Press <strong>View</strong> to see them.</p></div></div>
        <div class="hc-option"><div class="hc-option-icon is-info"><x-icon name="transfer" /></div><div><div class="hc-option-title">Schedule changed</div><p>A group you sit on moved to another room, date or time.</p></div></div>
        <div class="hc-option"><div class="hc-option-icon"><x-icon name="repeat" /></div><div><div class="hc-option-title">Replaced on panel</div><p>Someone took your seat on a group (for example a backup at the room device).</p></div></div>
        <div class="hc-option"><div class="hc-option-icon"><x-icon name="user-check" /></div><div><div class="hc-option-title">Unavailability approved</div><p>Your Mark Unavailable report was handled and a replacement assigned.</p></div></div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="hc-topic" id="pn-schedule">
    <h3><x-icon name="calendar" /> View Schedule</h3>
    <p>The same live schedule and queue the students see (<a href="#st-schedule">Viewing the schedule and queue</a>), for any of your categories: room tabs, search, Scheduled / Completed / Deferred lists, the group presenting now and who is next. Searching a group also shows its assigned panelists.</p>
</div>

<div class="hc-topic" id="pn-roles">
    <h3><x-icon name="crown" /> Lead Panelist, Member and Backup</h3>
    <div class="hc-options">
        <div class="hc-option"><div class="hc-option-icon"><x-icon name="crown" /></div><div><div class="hc-option-title">Lead Panelist (Chair)</div><p>Evaluates, and runs the room: Call Next, payment verification, Start, Pause, Complete, Defer and breaks. The Lead's remark becomes the group's official outcome. One per group.</p></div></div>
        <div class="hc-option"><div class="hc-option-icon is-info"><x-icon name="user-check" /></div><div><div class="hc-option-title">Member</div><p>Evaluates every group on the panel from their own device.</p></div></div>
        <div class="hc-option"><div class="hc-option-icon is-success"><x-icon name="user-plus" /></div><div><div class="hc-option-title">Backup Panelist</div><p>On standby. Can take an assigned panelist's seat at the room device when they cannot attend.</p></div></div>
    </div>
    <p>Lead powers follow the <strong>person</strong>, not the device: whichever terminal the Lead signs in to gets the controls.</p>
</div>

<div class="hc-topic" id="pn-join">
    <h3><x-icon name="qr-code" /> Joining a room terminal</h3>
    <p>Each room has one device per panel seat, already set up by the Administrator (<a href="#rd-setup">Setting up a device</a>). An empty device shows a QR code and a sign-in form. Join it one of two ways:</p>
    <figure class="hc-figure">
        <div class="hc-window">
            <div class="hc-window-bar"><div class="hc-window-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="hc-window-url">/room-session/home · Room 101 · Terminal 2</div></div>
            <div class="hc-screen is-tinted">
                <div class="m-grid-2" style="grid-template-columns:1.3fr 1fr;align-items:start;">
                    <div class="m-col">
                        <div class="m-card"><div class="m-label">Current Group</div><div class="m-bold">CFD-2026-0007</div><div class="m-small m-muted">Smart Campus Navigation App</div></div>
                        <div class="m-card"><div class="m-label">Room Queue</div>
                            <table class="m-table"><tbody>
                                <tr><td>5</td><td>CFD-2026-0012</td><td>9:20 AM</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>6</td><td>CFD-2026-0003</td><td>9:40 AM</td></tr>
                            </tbody></table>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="m-card" style="text-align:center;">
                        <div class="m-bold">Scan to Join <span class="m-pin">1</span></div>
                        <div style="display:grid;place-items:center;margin:.4rem 0;">
                            <div class="m-qr">@foreach (str_split('111001111101010101111001111000110000101101011010010110111010101101001010111011101') as $bit)<i class="{{ $bit === '1' ? '' : 'o' }}"></i>@endforeach</div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="m-xs m-muted">Or Log In Directly <span class="m-pin">2</span></div>
                        <div class="m-col" style="margin-top:.3rem;"><span class="m-input is-empty">Username</span><span class="m-input is-empty">Password</span><span class="m-btn is-block">Log In</span></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption><strong>Figure 9.</strong> An empty room terminal waiting for its panelist.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="hc-options-or">
        <div class="hc-option"><div class="hc-option-icon"><x-icon name="smartphone" /></div><div><div class="hc-option-title"><span class="m-pin">1</span> Scan QR Code</div><p>On your phone, sign in to your own panelist account, tap the <x-icon name="qr-code" style="width:.9em;height:.9em;vertical-align:-.1em" /> Room Session button in the top bar, point the camera at the device's code, then press <strong>Join This Terminal?</strong> → confirm. You can also scan with the phone's normal camera app. The code refreshes every few minutes.</p></div></div>
        <div class="hc-or">or</div>
        <div class="hc-option"><div class="hc-option-icon"><x-icon name="key" /></div><div><div class="hc-option-title"><span class="m-pin">2</span> Log In Directly</div><p>Type <strong>your own</strong> username and password into the device's form. Never use the room account here.</p></div></div>
    </div>
    <p>Once connected the device shows your name and badges:</p>
    <div class="hc-panel">
        <div class="hc-legend-row"><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-success">Can Evaluate</span><span>You are seated on the current group and can rate it.</span></div>
        <div class="hc-legend-row"><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-brand">Flow Control (Chair)</span><span>You are the Lead Panelist — the Presentation Controls appear.</span></div>
        <div class="hc-legend-row"><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-info">Alternate Panel</span><span>You are a backup on this room.</span></div>
        <div class="hc-legend-row"><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-muted">Not Assigned</span><span>You are not on this panel; see <a href="#pn-substitute">Backups and substitutions</a>.</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hc-note hc-note-warn"><x-icon name="alert-triangle" /><p>When you leave the room, press <strong>Log Out</strong> on the device so the next panelist can sit. You cannot be connected to two seats in the same room.</p></div>
</div>

<div class="hc-topic" id="pn-evaluate">
    <h3><x-icon name="clipboard-check" /> Evaluating a group</h3>
    <p>When a group is called, the evaluation sheet opens on every connected panelist's device. It is the same sheet the Administrator built in the Evaluation Library.</p>
    <figure class="hc-figure">
        <div class="hc-window">
            <div class="hc-window-bar"><div class="hc-window-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="hc-window-url">Evaluation · CFD-2026-0012</div></div>
            <div class="hc-screen is-tinted">
                <div class="m-paper">
                    <div class="m-between"><span class="m-bold">Capstone Title: Smart Campus Navigation App</span></div>
                    <table class="m-table" style="margin-top:.4rem;">
                        <thead><tr><th>Performance Indicators</th><th>Rating (1–5) <span class="m-pin">1</span></th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td class="m-bold">I. Presentation (20%)</td><td></td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Clarity of delivery</td><td><span class="m-bubbles"><i>1</i><i>2</i><i>3</i><i class="is-on">4</i><i>5</i></span></td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Mastery of the subject</td><td><span class="m-bubbles"><i>1</i><i>2</i><i>3</i><i>4</i><i class="is-on">5</i></span></td></tr>
                            <tr><td class="m-bold">II. System Functionality (30%)</td><td></td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Features work as specified</td><td><span class="m-bubbles"><i>1</i><i>2</i><i>3</i><i>4</i><i>5</i></span></td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                    <div class="m-grid-2" style="margin-top:.5rem;">
                        <div><div class="m-label">Researchers · Individual <span class="m-pin">2</span></div><div class="m-between m-small"><span>Dela Cruz, Juan</span><span class="m-input" style="width:2.6rem">92</span></div><div class="m-between m-small" style="margin-top:.2rem"><span>Reyes, Ana</span><span class="m-input" style="width:2.6rem">90</span></div></div>
                        <div><div class="m-label">Remarks <span class="m-pin">3</span></div>
                            <div class="m-row m-small"><span class="m-check is-on"></span> Pass with Minor Revision</div>
                            <div class="m-row m-small"><span class="m-check"></span> Re-Defense</div>
                            <div class="m-row m-small"><span class="m-check"></span> Failed</div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="m-between" style="margin-top:.5rem;"><span class="m-small">Total Score: <b>84.67</b> / 100</span><span class="m-row"><span class="m-btn"><x-icon name="send" /> Submit Evaluation</span><span class="m-pin">4</span></span></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption><strong>Figure 10.</strong> The evaluation sheet on a room device (Standard mode).</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <ul class="hc-pins">
        <li><span class="m-pin">1</span><span><strong>Rate every criterion</strong> from 1 (Very Insufficient) to 5 (Very Sufficient). Each tap is saved immediately.</span></li>
        <li><span class="m-pin">2</span><span><strong>Individual score</strong> for each researcher, 0–100 (Standard mode).</span></li>
        <li><span class="m-pin">3</span><span><strong>Remarks</strong> — choose one outcome, and add comments if needed.</span></li>
        <li><span class="m-pin">4</span><span><strong>Submit Evaluation</strong> — available once every required part is filled.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="hc-note hc-note-danger"><x-icon name="lock" /><p><span class="hc-note-title">Submitting is final.</span> A submitted evaluation cannot be edited. Review your ratings before you submit.</p></div>
    <h4>Title Proposal mode</h4>
    <p>The criteria repeat once for each proposed title. Rate each title, and tick <strong>Approved</strong> on the title the panel accepts. There are no individual scores or total in this mode.</p>
</div>

<div class="hc-topic" id="pn-control">
    <h3><x-icon name="play" /> Running the room (Lead Panelist)</h3>
    <p>When you are signed in as the Lead, <strong>Presentation Controls</strong> appear on your device:</p>
    <figure class="hc-figure">
        <div class="hc-window">
            <div class="hc-window-bar"><div class="hc-window-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="hc-window-url">Presentation Controls · Room 101</div></div>
            <div class="hc-screen is-tinted">
                <div class="m-grid-2" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1.2fr;align-items:start;">
                    <div class="m-card">
                        <div class="m-between"><span class="m-label">Current Group</span><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-success">Ongoing</span></div>
                        <div class="m-bold">CFD-2026-0012</div>
                        <div class="m-timer" style="color:var(--hc-success)">14:22</div>
                        <div class="m-small m-muted">Payment: <span class="hc-badge hc-badge-success">Verified</span></div>
                        <div class="m-blink m-small" style="margin-top:.3rem;"><x-icon name="coffee" style="width:.8rem;height:.8rem" /> Scheduled break at 12:00 PM</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="m-card">
                        <div class="m-label" style="margin-bottom:.35rem;">Presentation Controls</div>
                        <div class="m-control-grid">
                            <div class="m-control is-disabled"><x-icon name="megaphone" />Call Next</div>
                            <div class="m-control is-disabled"><x-icon name="play" />Start</div>
                            <div class="m-control"><x-icon name="pause" />Pause</div>
                            <div class="m-control is-primary"><x-icon name="check" />Complete</div>
                            <div class="m-control is-danger"><x-icon name="defer" />Defer</div>
                            <div class="m-control"><x-icon name="coffee" />Scheduled Break</div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption><strong>Figure 11.</strong> The Lead Panelist's controls while a group presents.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <ol class="hc-steps">
        <li class="hc-step"><div class="hc-step-marker">1</div><div class="hc-step-body"><div class="hc-step-head"><x-icon name="megaphone" /> Call Next</div><p class="hc-step-text">Calls the next group in the queue. Locked until <strong>every terminal in the room has a panelist connected</strong>, and while the room is on a break.</p><div class="hc-result">Group <x-icon name="arrow-right" /> <span class="hc-badge hc-badge-brand">Called</span></div></div></li>
        <li class="hc-step"><div class="hc-step-marker">2</div><div class="hc-step-body"><div class="hc-step-head"><x-icon name="wallet" /> Verify payment (if required)</div><p class="hc-step-text">Type each receipt's reference number and press <strong>Verify</strong>, one row per payment type. A number already used anywhere in the system is refused and the screen says which group holds it.</p></div></li>
        <li class="hc-step"><div class="hc-step-marker">3</div><div class="hc-step-body"><div class="hc-step-head"><x-icon name="play" /> Start</div><p class="hc-step-text">Starts the presentation timer. Locked until every payment type is verified.</p><div class="hc-result">Group <x-icon name="arrow-right" /> <span class="hc-badge hc-badge-success">Ongoing</span></div></div></li>
        <li class="hc-step"><div class="hc-step-marker">4</div><div class="hc-step-body"><div class="hc-step-head"><x-icon name="pause" /> Pause / Resume</div><p class="hc-step-text">Stops the clock for an interruption; paused time does not count against the group. Going over the time limit is allowed — the timer turns red and shows the extra time.</p></div></li>
        <li class="hc-step"><div class="hc-step-marker">5</div><div class="hc-step-body"><div class="hc-step-head"><x-icon name="check" /> Complete</div><p class="hc-step-text">Ends the presentation. Locked until <strong>every panelist has submitted</strong> an evaluation. Your remark becomes the official outcome.</p><div class="hc-result">Group <x-icon name="arrow-right" /> <span class="hc-badge hc-badge-success">Completed</span></div></div></li>
    </ol>
    <h4>Deferring a group</h4>
    <p>Use <strong>Defer This Group</strong> when the called or presenting group cannot go on. Pick a reason (Not Present When Called, Incomplete Group, Not Ready to Present, System / Prototype Not Working, Incomplete Requirements, Payment Not Verified) and press <strong>Confirm Defer</strong>. The group leaves the active queue, the Administrators are notified, and you can call the next group.</p>
    <div class="hc-note hc-note-info"><x-icon name="info" /><p>If the Administrator moves or defers the group you have <strong>called</strong> (but not started), every device shows a notice such as "CFD-2026-0012 was moved by …. Call the next group." Pressing Call Next clears it. A group that is already presenting cannot be changed by anyone but you.</p></div>
</div>

<div class="hc-topic" id="pn-breaks">
    <h3><x-icon name="coffee" /> Scheduled breaks</h3>
    <p>A room can have planned breaks (lunch, for example). The schedule places no group across a break.</p>
    <div class="hc-options">
        <div class="hc-option"><div class="hc-option-icon is-danger"><x-icon name="alert-triangle" /></div><div><div class="hc-option-title">Warning</div><p>While a group is up and another one would not fit before the break, every device shows a blinking red "Scheduled break at …" under the timer.</p></div></div>
        <div class="hc-option"><div class="hc-option-icon"><x-icon name="clock" /></div><div><div class="hc-option-title">Group still presenting at break time</div><p>The Lead is asked: <strong>Cancel Break</strong> (no break today; continue straight on) or <strong>Finish Group, Then Break</strong> (the break still ends at its planned time). Doing nothing behaves like the second.</p></div></div>
        <div class="hc-option"><div class="hc-option-icon is-info"><x-icon name="coffee" /></div><div><div class="hc-option-title">Room on break</div><p>The room shows <span class="hc-badge hc-badge-info">Break</span> and the controls lock. The Lead can press <strong>End Break</strong> to resume early; otherwise it ends by itself.</p></div></div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="hc-topic" id="pn-substitute">
    <h3><x-icon name="repeat" /> Backups and substitutions</h3>
    <p>If you sign in to a terminal for a group you are not seated on, the device asks whose seat you are taking:</p>
    <div class="hc-options-or">
        <div class="hc-option"><div class="hc-option-icon is-success"><x-icon name="user-plus" /></div><div><div class="hc-option-title">You are the Backup</div><p>Choose the assigned panelist you are filling in for. The swap happens immediately; if they were the Lead, you become the Lead. They are notified.</p></div></div>
        <div class="hc-or">or</div>
        <div class="hc-option"><div class="hc-option-icon"><x-icon name="user-check" /></div><div><div class="hc-option-title">You are not on this panel</div><p>Choose the panelist you are replacing. The device shows "Waiting for an Administrator to review your request…" until an Administrator confirms or rejects it.</p></div></div>
    </div>
</div>
